{
  "$schema": "../../scenario.schema.json",
  "id": "author-images/a-copy-of-a-media-or-location-label-reads-as-the-runtime-s",
  "title": "A participant's copy of a media's or a location's label reaches a model as the runtime's own label does, whether it sees or not",
  "rules": [
    "§6.4",
    "§6.6"
  ],
  "requirements": [
    "RK-6.4-295",
    "RK-6.6-026"
  ],
  "notes": "No mark (RFC §6.4): the label the runtime writes for a media or a location stands inside its sender's own message and names what that sender gave (a caption, a file name, coordinates), so a copy claims nothing more than that sender could send, where a mark speaks for the runtime or the application. Python's _media.py media_label and location_label write the labels; a model that sees reads a media that is no image as its label too. Two rooms, one model that does not see and one that sees, the same four messages: a text holding copies of both labels, a PDF, prose holding their words, and a location, last so that it is each model's input.",
  "setup": {
    "channels": [
      {
        "id": "ws",
        "type": "websocket",
        "category": "transport"
      },
      {
        "id": "blind",
        "type": "ai",
        "model": {
          "rounds": [
            {
              "text": "Read 0."
            },
            {
              "text": "Read 1."
            },
            {
              "text": "Read 2."
            },
            {
              "text": "Read 3."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "sees",
        "type": "ai",
        "model": {
          "vision": true,
          "rounds": [
            {
              "text": "Read 0."
            },
            {
              "text": "Read 1."
            },
            {
              "text": "Read 2."
            },
            {
              "text": "Read 3."
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    ],
    "rooms": [
      {
        "id": "room-1",
        "bindings": [
          {
            "channel_id": "ws"
          },
          {
            "channel_id": "blind",
            "category": "intelligence"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "room-2",
        "bindings": [
          {
            "channel_id": "ws"
          },
          {
            "channel_id": "sees",
            "category": "intelligence"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "steps": [
